---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import InstallButton from '../components/InstallButton.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'About TokGrid — Independent TikTok Analytics Extension';
const description =
  'TokGrid is an independent, local-first Chrome extension for organizing public TikTok page data. Learn what it does, why it is scoped, and what it refuses to claim.';
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'About', href: '/about/' },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/about/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="container-page py-10 sm:py-14">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { name: 'About', href: '/about/' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-600">
          About
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">
          About TokGrid
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
          TokGrid is an independent Chrome extension for turning public TikTok page data
          into a clearer, reviewable sample. It does not decide what the data means for
          you — it makes the sample easier to inspect, filter, and take with you.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-7">
          <InstallButton campaign="about" label="Add to Chrome" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page grid gap-12 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem]">
    <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <h2>What TokGrid is</h2>
      <p>
        TokGrid is a browser extension for people who research public TikTok content:
        sellers and product researchers, content marketers, creators, and analysts. It
        organizes the videos and product anchors that are already loaded in the page into
        a data list, a sample analytics view, a product view, and export/download
        workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        The product is built around a simple constraint: work with the page the user has
        opened, not a hidden database or a background crawler. The extension reads what
        the page has already rendered, using read-only page data. It does not overwrite{' '}
        <code>fetch</code> or <code>XMLHttpRequest</code>, does not intercept network
        requests, and does not make TikTok API calls to collect data.
      </p>

      <h2>Why local-first matters</h2>
      <p>
        Many research tools require you to send page data to a server or log in to a
        separate dashboard. TokGrid keeps page processing in the browser. That reduces
        the number of places your research data can go, and it keeps the workflow close to
        the page where the data appears.
      </p>
      <p>
        Local-first is not the same as “no network requests ever.” Downloads contact
        TikTok media domains when you click them, and subscription validation contacts a
        license server. Those flows are narrow and separate from page data collection.
        The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains each one.
      </p>

      <h2>What TokGrid deliberately does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It does not promise a complete account history or a complete TikTok database.</li>
        <li>It does not bypass login, CAPTCHA, rate limits, DRM, or other access controls.</li>
        <li>It does not estimate sales, revenue, advertising performance, or virality.</li>
        <li>It does not provide creator ratings, automated outreach, or deep cross-creator comparison.</li>
        <li>It does not merge data across pages or store historical snapshots in this version.</li>
        <li>It does not claim affiliation with TikTok or ByteDance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Current platform: TikTok</h2>
      <p>
        The current build supports public TikTok pages: Home, For You, and Following;
        video detail; hashtags; search results; user profiles; Explore; and music detail
        video lists. The extension is designed for logged-out public pages. It does not
        support private or logged-in-only content.
      </p>
      <p>
        The interface is available in 30 languages and follows the browser’s UI language.
        The current extension version is <strong>{SITE.version}</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Long-term direction</h2>
      <p>
        The broader direction is Social Media Data Intelligence: helping people organize
        public social content into data they can reason about. That is a direction, not a
        claim that other platforms are supported today. TokGrid currently supports TikTok
        only, and any future platform coverage should be announced only when it is
        actually available.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        TokGrid is an independent product. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        sponsored by TikTok or ByteDance. TikTok and related marks are trademarks of
        their respective owners.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/70 p-6">
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <Icon name="info" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-700" />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-950">A note on the website</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
              This website is a static product site. It does not currently load analytics
              or tracking scripts by default. Screenshot positions are labelled until real
              product captures are supplied.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-950">At a glance</h2>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-slate-500">Product</dt>
            <dd class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Chrome extension</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-slate-500">Current version</dt>
            <dd class="font-semibold text-slate-900">{SITE.version}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-slate-500">Platform</dt>
            <dd class="font-semibold text-slate-900">TikTok, public pages only</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-slate-500">Processing</dt>
            <dd class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Local-first page data</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-slate-500">Interface</dt>
            <dd class="font-semibold text-slate-900">30 languages</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-950">Related</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/features/" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-brand-700">Features</a></li>
          <li><a href="/guides/" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-brand-700">Guides</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-brand-700">Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/support/" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-brand-700">Support</a></li>
          <li><a href="/changelog/" class="text-slate-600 hover:text-brand-700">Changelog</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <CTA
    campaign="about-final"
    title="Work from the page you already have open."
    description="Install TokGrid and start with the free core features. Pro adds batch downloads and structured export."
    secondaryHref="/guides/"
    secondaryLabel="Read the guides"
  />
</BaseLayout>
